\textbf{Generator.} The 100-dimensional noise vector is passed through a Dense layer with
$7\times7\times128$ units and reshaped into a $7\times7\times128$ feature map. Two
transposed convolution layers with stride 2 then increase the size from $7\times7$ to
$14\times14$ and then to $28\times28$. A final transposed convolution layer with a Tanh
activation produces a $28\times28\times1$ image with pixel values in $[-1,1]$. Batch
normalization and LeakyReLU are used in the hidden layers to stabilize training
(Table~\ref{tab:gen}).

\textbf{Discriminator.} The Discriminator takes a $28\times28\times1$ image and uses two
strided convolution layers to reduce it to $14\times14$ and then $7\times7$ feature maps.
LeakyReLU activations and Dropout (0.3) are used after each convolution. The result is
flattened and passed to a single Dense unit that outputs a logit (a raw score) for real or
fake. No Sigmoid is used in the model, because the loss function is configured with
\texttt{from\_logits=True} (Table~\ref{tab:disc}).

