% ======================= 7. EVALUATION =======================
\section{Evaluation Metrics}
A GAN has no single correct output, and its loss values do not behave like the loss of a
classifier, so accuracy cannot be used. The system was evaluated in the following ways.
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item \textbf{Loss curves:} the Generator and Discriminator losses were plotted over all
        epochs. Curves that stay in a similar range, without one network completely
        dominating, indicate that training is balanced.
  \item \textbf{Visual inspection:} image grids from different epochs were checked to see
        whether clothing shapes (shirts, shoes, bags and so on) become recognizable and
        whether the images contain noise or broken regions.
  \item \textbf{Diversity check:} the grids were checked for repeated images or a single
        dominant category, which would indicate mode collapse.
\end{itemize}
No quantitative image-quality metric such as the Fr\'echet Inception Distance (FID) was
computed, so the quality was judged visually only.

